k chain. Each attempt is tried in order of specificity:\\n- Most specific: File paths (direct file system validation)\\n- Medium: Literal string \\"adhoc\\" (explicit keyword)\\n- Most general: Dynamic imports (flexible but requires runtime evaluation)\\n\\nThe pattern allows the method to:\\n- Avoid expensive operations (like import attempts) when simpler validations (file path checks) succeed\\n- Provide clear error messages at each stage (each validation can raise specific `click.BadParameter` exceptions)\\n- Maintain a single entry point that handles multiple input types without requiring the caller to know the input format in advance\\n\\nThis design is used by the `--cert` option in Flask\'s `run` command (line 887), allowing users to specify certificates as file paths, use ad-hoc certificates for development, or import pre-configured SSLContext objects from their code."}' + '\n')
